WEBVTT

NOTE
This audio description covers the opening of Ultimecia's Castle interior.
Duration: approximately 28 seconds
Scene: Gothic, surreal castle architecture with time-distorted elements.
For blind players: Descriptions focus on spatial layout, architectural details, and atmosphere.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Squall and his team stand at the entrance of Ultimecia's Castle interior. The space is vast and cathedral-like, dominated by towering columns and soaring Gothic arches. Elaborate crystal chandeliers hang from a ceiling that seems impossibly distant, their light casting long shadows across polished marble floors. The walls are adorned with distorted portraits in ornate frames — the painted figures within them appear twisted and grotesque, as if trapped in warped time.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A grand staircase dominates the chamber, but its geometry is unnatural. The stairs ascend at impossible angles — some sections slope sideways, others seem to fold back on themselves. The bannister is wrought iron, intricate and beautiful yet deeply unsettling. The team moves forward cautiously, their footsteps echoing in the empty space.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
To the left, a ballroom is visible through archways, its floor a perfect mirror of polished black marble. Crystal fixtures line the walls. The room is empty yet it feels watched, haunted. To the right, clock towers with gears visible through glass faces dominate the architecture. The clocks all show different times, and their ticking is audible but discordant — out of sync with each other.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The team ventures deeper into the castle's heart. Rooms connect in ways that defy logic — corridors lead to chambers that shouldn't exist in normal space. The atmosphere is oppressive and heavy. Purple and dark blue magical auras cling to the stone surfaces. The air feels thick with compressed time itself. The team is moving toward the ultimate confrontation, their resolve hardening as they progress into this heart of darkness.
